{"type":"begin","data":{"path":{"text":"en.wikipedia.org/Dollhouse (TV series) - Wikipedia.txt"}}}
{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"en.wikipedia.org/Dollhouse (TV series) - Wikipedia.txt"},"lines":{"text":"The series stars Eliza Dushku, who worked with Whedon on Buffy the Vampire Slayer and Angel. Elizabeth Craft and Sarah Fain were the showrunners, while Jane Espenson, Tim Minear and Steven S. DeKnight served as consulting producers. In addition to Joss Whedon, the writing staff included Tim Minear, Jed Whedon (Joss' brother), Maurissa Tancharoen (Jed's wife), Andrew Chambliss, Tracy Bellomo, Elizabeth Craft and Sarah Fain. Whedon directed a number of his own episodes, as he has done for many of the shows he created. Tim Minear and Buffy producer David Solomon also directed. Fox used a viral marketing campaign to promote Dollhouse in May 2008.\n"},"line_number":49,"absolute_offset":8872,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"consulting producer"},"start":211,"end":230}]}}
